      "shadow_camera_margin_to_reproduce": -0.128,
      "observation": "The trained backbone stays at ceiling while the RANDOM backbone loses 0.063 AUC on average (up to 0.206 on pendulum). Margin (real - random) therefore *increases* in 6/7 scenarios (mean +0.0594), whereas the shadow_camera anomaly that S4 set out to explain has margin -0.1280. Synthetic camera motion in this range does not reproduce the anomaly's signature even in sign. Subject to the same 27% magnitude caveat, so it is a directional observation, not a refutation.",
