        "text": "The AUC-margin increase reported in S4_verdict.json is at least partly a ceiling asymmetry: real AUC is pinned at 1.0000 and cannot fall, while random AUC has headroom. On the unsaturated d' readout real retains 0.754 of its level-0 separation and random retains 0.656, i.e. both degrade comparably, so 'the trained backbone is robust to camera motion' is NOT supported once the ceiling is removed"
